// Directing to greeting
-> greeting

=== greeting ===
Ah, Barrington. I’m glad you made it out of the forest! It’s feeling dark down here. You look weary, my friend.

I hope I can be of some help. I came across a hunk of wood here. I hear you’re building yourself a ship! It would be good for you to let yourself out of this place.

One scientist to another, sometimes the solution we have simply is not enough. We have to try something else.

If you’ve outgrown this place here, why not try something new yourself? There’s always an alternative! 

When you leave this place, what’s something else you might try?
* [I'm going to become an artist!] -> artist
* [I'll write a story about adventure!] -> story
* [I think I'll get into music!] -> music


=== artist === 
What a great idea! Creative expression is a great way to work out these different solutions. 
-> farewell

=== story === 
Brilliant! I know you'll have some amazing stories to tell!
-> farewell

=== music ===
Amazing! Music is a wonderful kind of expression. I predict you'll be great at it.
-> farewell

=== farewell === 
You have a brilliant mind Barrington, I hypothesize you will find success wherever you go.

Good luck!
-> END